    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "The team now wants a model to predict the ultraviolet (UV) index based on the hour of the day. This time, you’ll need to import anything you need, build and train a model, then test it.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Import `LinearRegression` from `scikit-learn`’s `linear_model` module.\r\n2. Create a new, untrained linear regression model.\r\n3. Train it on the inputs (hours) and outputs (UV levels).\r\n4. Compute the model’s prediction for the UV level at 3 pm (hour 15) and at 11 pm (hour 23) and print each prediction. Then, print the actual UV level recorded in the dataset for 3 pm and 11 pm.\r\n5. Run the program and compare the line with the readings, as in Level 1.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nTo import a class in Python, use code like from `sklearn.<module>` import `<Class>`.\r\n\r\nOnce you’ve created a model, `model.fit` trains it on a dataset of inputs and outputs.\r\n\r\nThe `uv_levels` list stores all of the UV levels from the training data, sorted by hour. `uv_levels[0]` is the UV level recorded at midnight.",
